Read the signed columns before the absolute ones. If images-only is systematically
ABOVE the truth at low deciles, its advantage there is |x| upward bias from two studies
and any shrinkage flatters the mixed arm for free. The interpretable cells are then the
top deciles, where that bias is negligible.

The count-0 row is not a null check after all: a coordinate study that reported nothing
near a voxel still enters the censoring term, so its SILENCE contributes there even with
no focus reaching. That makes count-0 the largest and most interesting stratum rather
than a control -- but it is also where the |x| confound bites hardest.
